[S2] The End

// Timer accepts seconds or a size: XS, S, M, L, XL.
[A1] Timer{1} ->(T1)

[P] Vee -> Gee
[T1]
[1] Is that it? ->(C1)

// The fact stored in A3 is still there the second time the story reaches this group, so the else only runs once.
[C1]
[1] if(CF{second-act}) D1
[2] T2

[P] Gee -> Vee
[T2]
[1] That was the last line.
[2] From here it goes back to the top. ->(T3)

[P] Vee -> Gee
[T3]
[1] Then we leave before it does. ->(A2)

// Both walk out together; the story goes on once Vee is out.
[A2] Move{Vee, Door} &(Move{Gee, Door}) ->(A3)

// Store the fact and start scene 1 again.
[A3] AddFact{second-act} ->(FE2BFF200C6F409E8B737C0C69ADB42D /*The Room S1-A1*/)

[P] Gee -> Vee
[D1]
[1] 'Let's go.' ->(T4)
[2] {hold} 'Let's wait.' ->(T5)

[T4]
[1] Let's go. ->(A4)

[A4] Move{Vee, Door} &(Move{Gee, Door}) ->(A5)

[T5]
[1] Let's wait. ->(T6)

[P] Vee -> Gee
[T6]
[1] For what? ->(T7)

[P] Gee -> Vee
[T7]
[1] For someone to pick. ->(A5)

// An action with nothing after it ends its own branch:
// Print ends here, while &(...) has already started the talk alongside it.
[A5] Print{Showcase finished} &(T8)

// Nested flows put a pause between talks. The last talk leads back to the first, so they keep talking
// until the player restarts. "vgs travel" reports a loop that nothing leads out of: here it is on purpose.
[P] Gee -> Vee
[T8]
[1] So. ->(Timer{S} ->(T9))

[P] Vee -> Gee
[T9]
[1] So. ->(Timer{L} ->(T10))

[P] Gee -> Vee
[T10]
[1] Do you think they're still there? ->(Timer{S} ->(T11))

[P] Vee -> Gee
[T11]
[1] We're still talking, aren't we? ->(Timer{L} ->(T12))

[T12]
[1] Say something new. ->(Timer{S} ->(T13))

[P] Gee -> Vee
[T13]
[1] Something new. ->(Timer{S} ->(T14))

[P] Vee -> Gee
[T14]
[1] Not like that. ->(Timer{L} ->(T15))

[P] Gee -> Vee
[T15]
[1] We could go. ->(Timer{M} ->(T16))

[P] Vee -> Gee
[T16]
[1] We could. ->(Timer{L} ->(T17))

[P] Gee -> Vee
[T17]
[1] Have we said all this before? ->(Timer{S} ->(T18))

[P] Vee -> Gee
[T18]
[1] Only every time. ->(Timer{L} ->(T8))